/** @I18n.EnLegal.Catalog — English text of the policies and the about page */
module I18n.EnLegal

/// English policy messages by key.
export const MESSAGES: Map[Str, Str] = mapOf([
    ("legal.version", "Version :version · Effective October 10, 2026"),
    ("legal.contents", "On this page"),
    ("legal.summary_title", "In short"),
    ("legal.terms.title", "Terms of Use"),
    ("legal.terms.description", "The agreement between you and Boricua Experience: who may use the platform, how activities are published and joined, and what each of us is responsible for."),
    ("legal.terms.intro", "These terms are the agreement between you and Boricua Experience for using the website and app. By creating an account, or by using the platform without one, you accept them. We have tried to write them so they can be read in one sitting."),
    ("legal.terms.summary", "Boricua Experience is for adults 18 and over. Organizers are responsible for the activities they publish; we provide the place to find and join them, not the activities themselves. Treat people with respect, keep information honest, and use your judgment when you meet people in person."),
    ("legal.terms.service.title", "What Boricua Experience is"),
    ("legal.terms.service.body", "Boricua Experience is a platform where people in Puerto Rico discover activities, publish their own, and ask to join activities other people organize. Activities are created and run by members of the community.\n\nWe do not organize, supervise, insure, or attend the activities listed on the platform, and we are not a party to any arrangement between an organizer and the people who attend. When this document says “organizer”, it means the member who published an activity; “attendee” means a member who asked to join one."),
    ("legal.terms.eligibility.title", "Who may use it"),
    ("legal.terms.eligibility.body", "You must be at least 18 years old to create an account, publish an activity, or ask to join one. When you sign up we ask for your date of birth to confirm this; we do not keep the date itself, only the fact that you met the requirement.\n\nIn Puerto Rico the age of majority is 21. If you are between 18 and 20, you confirm that you may enter into this agreement under the laws that apply to you. The service is free, and nothing in it requires you to take on a financial obligation through us.\n\nYou may hold only one account, it must be in your own name, and the information you give us must be accurate. You may not use the platform if we have previously closed your account for breaking these terms."),
    ("legal.terms.account.title", "Your account"),
    ("legal.terms.account.body", "You can sign in with an email address and password or with a Google account. You are responsible for everything that happens under your account, so keep your password private and change it right away, using account recovery, if you think someone else has used it.\n\nYou can pause your account, which hides your profile and activities, or delete it permanently, at any time from your account settings."),
    ("legal.terms.publishing.title", "Publishing an activity"),
    ("legal.terms.publishing.body", "When you publish an activity you decide its visibility (public, link only, or private), whether requests need your approval, its capacity, its price, and where and when it happens. The exact address is shown only to the people you approve; everyone else sees an approximate area.\n\nAs the organizer you are responsible for the activity: that what you describe is accurate and kept up to date, that you have any permit, permission, or insurance the activity requires, that you follow the rules of the venue and the laws of Puerto Rico, including those on alcohol, noise, the use of beaches and natural reserves, and public gatherings, and that you take reasonable care for the safety of the people who attend.\n\nIf an activity has a price, payment is arranged directly between you and the attendees. Boricua Experience does not process payments, hold money, or handle refunds, and any refund policy is yours to state and honor. If you cancel or change an activity, do it on the platform so attendees are notified."),
    ("legal.terms.joining.title", "Asking to join"),
    ("legal.terms.joining.body", "When you ask to join an activity, the organizer sees your name, profile photo, town, and the message you write. The organizer decides who is approved. Once you are approved you see the exact place and any instructions, and, unless you turn it off in your settings, other approved attendees can see that you are going.\n\nIf your plans change, withdraw your request so your place can go to someone else. Follow the organizer's instructions and the rules of the place where the activity happens."),
    ("legal.terms.minors.title", "Minors and family activities"),
    ("legal.terms.minors.body", "Accounts are only for adults. People under 18 may not register, publish, or ask to join activities, and they may not use another person's account.\n\nActivities may not be aimed primarily at minors. An organizer may welcome families, but then every minor must attend with a parent or legal guardian who has an account, asks to join on the minor's behalf, and remains responsible for the minor throughout the activity. Organizers must not use the platform to collect names, photos, or contact details of minors, and profile photos must show the account holder, not a child.\n\nIf we learn that an account belongs to someone under 18, we close it and delete its information as described in the Privacy Policy. If you believe a minor is using the platform, or that an activity puts minors at risk, report it using the “Involves minors” reason. Reports about minors are reviewed first."),
    ("legal.terms.conduct.title", "How we treat each other"),
    ("legal.terms.conduct.body", "Boricua Experience works because people can trust what they find on it and the people they meet through it. You agree not to publish false or misleading activities; not to harass, threaten, or discriminate against anyone, including on the basis of race, color, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, disability, or age; not to post sexual content or content that promotes violence or illegal activity; not to send spam, advertising nobody asked for, or scams; not to impersonate anyone; and not to collect other members' information to use outside the platform.\n\nYou also agree not to interfere with how the platform works, including by scraping it, probing it for weaknesses, or creating accounts automatically."),
    ("legal.terms.safety.title", "Meeting people and taking part"),
    ("legal.terms.safety.body", "We do not run background checks on members, and we cannot guarantee the identity, intentions, or conduct of anyone you meet through the platform. Use your judgment: meet in public places when you can, tell someone where you are going, and leave any situation that feels wrong.\n\nMany activities in Puerto Rico take place outdoors, at beaches, rivers, trails, and on the water, where conditions change quickly. Check official weather and safety alerts, respect closures and warnings, and do not take part in anything beyond your ability. You take part in activities voluntarily and at your own risk.\n\nIf you are in danger, call 911. Then report the activity or the member on the platform so we can act."),
    ("legal.terms.content.title", "What you publish"),
    ("legal.terms.content.body", "You keep ownership of the text and photos you publish. You give Boricua Experience a non-exclusive, royalty-free license to host, display, and adapt that content to run and show the platform, including in search results while an activity is public. The license ends when you delete the content or your account, except for copies we must keep for the reasons in the Privacy Policy.\n\nOnly publish content you have the right to share, and only photos of people who agreed to be shown."),
    ("legal.terms.moderation.title", "Reports and enforcement"),
    ("legal.terms.moderation.body", "Anyone can report an activity. We review reports and may hide or remove content, limit features, or suspend or close accounts that break these terms or put others at risk, and we may do so without notice when safety requires it. Where it is safe to do so, we let you know what happened.\n\nWe also cooperate with law enforcement when the law requires it or when someone's safety is at stake."),
    ("legal.terms.disclaimers.title", "What we do not promise"),
    ("legal.terms.disclaimers.body", "We work to keep the platform available and the information on it useful, but we provide it as it is and as available. We do not guarantee that it will be uninterrupted or free of errors, that any activity will take place as described, or that any member is who they say they are."),
    ("legal.terms.liability.title", "Limits of our responsibility"),
    ("legal.terms.liability.body", "To the extent the law allows, Boricua Experience is not responsible for what happens at activities organized by members, for the conduct of any member on or off the platform, or for indirect, incidental, or consequential losses arising from your use of the platform. Nothing in these terms limits a responsibility that the law does not allow us to limit."),
    ("legal.terms.indemnity.title", "Your responsibility to us"),
    ("legal.terms.indemnity.body", "If a claim is brought against Boricua Experience because of an activity you organized, content you published, or your breach of these terms or of the law, you agree to cover the reasonable costs that claim causes us, including legal fees, to the extent the law allows."),
    ("legal.terms.changes.title", "Changes to these terms"),
    ("legal.terms.changes.body", "We may update these terms as the platform changes. When a change is important we will tell you on the platform before it takes effect and ask you to accept the new version the next time you sign in. The version and effective date at the top of this page always show which terms apply."),
    ("legal.terms.law.title", "Governing law and disputes"),
    ("legal.terms.law.body", "These terms are governed by the laws of the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico and the applicable federal laws of the United States. If a disagreement arises, we ask that you first try to resolve it with us informally. If it cannot be resolved, it will be heard by the competent courts in San Juan, Puerto Rico, unless the law gives you the right to a different forum."),
    ("legal.terms.contact.title", "Talking to us"),
    ("legal.terms.contact.body", "To report an activity, use the report option on its page. To download, correct, or delete your information, use your account settings. Every request made there is recorded so we can show it was handled."),
    ("legal.privacy.title", "Privacy Policy"),
    ("legal.privacy.description", "What information Boricua Experience keeps, why, who can see it, how long we keep it, and how you control it."),
    ("legal.privacy.intro", "This policy explains what information Boricua Experience collects when you use the website and app, what we do with it, who can see it, and the choices you have. It applies to everyone who uses the platform, with or without an account."),
    ("legal.privacy.summary", "We keep what the platform needs and nothing more. We do not sell your information or show advertising. Your exact location is off until you turn it on and is never public. You can download or delete your information at any time from your account."),
    ("legal.privacy.scope.title", "Who we are"),
    ("legal.privacy.scope.body", "Boricua Experience operates the platform at boricuaexperience.com and is responsible for the information described here. Organizers who receive your information when you ask to join their activity are responsible for how they use it outside the platform."),
    ("legal.privacy.collect.title", "What we collect"),
    ("legal.privacy.collect.body", "When you create an account we keep your name, email address, preferred language, and, if you sign in with Google, the identifier Google gives us for your account. To confirm you are an adult we ask for your date of birth, check it at that moment, and keep only the fact that you are 18 or older.\n\nYour profile can also include a photo, a short bio, and your town; all of these are optional. As you use the platform we keep the activities you publish, the requests you send and the messages in them, the decisions organizers make, the activities you save, your likes and dislikes, the reports you file, and your notification and privacy settings.\n\nIf you turn on live location, we keep the positions your device shares while it is on. We also keep a record of the policies you accepted and of your cookie choices, and technical information our servers need to run securely: your IP address, the type of browser and device, and the time and result of each request."),
    ("legal.privacy.use.title", "How we use it"),
    ("legal.privacy.use.body", "We use your information to provide the platform: to show you activities, let organizers review requests, reveal the exact place to approved attendees, send the notifications you choose, and remind you before an activity starts. Your likes, saves, and town help us recommend activities you may enjoy; you can see and change them at any time.\n\nWe also use it to keep the platform safe, to investigate reports and prevent fraud and abuse, to keep records the law requires, and to understand, in aggregate, how the platform is used so we can improve it. We use your location only with your permission, and optional cookies only with your consent. We do not sell your information, and we do not use it for advertising."),
    ("legal.privacy.visibility.title", "What other people see"),
    ("legal.privacy.visibility.body", "Your public profile shows your name, photo, town, bio, and the public activities you organize. When you ask to join an activity, its organizer also sees your request message. Once you are approved, other approved attendees can see that you are going unless you hide yourself from attendee lists in your settings.\n\nYour email address, your date of birth, your precise location history, and your reports are never shown to other members."),
    ("legal.privacy.location.title", "Your location"),
    ("legal.privacy.location.body", "When you use “Near me”, your browser sends your position with that search so results can be sorted by distance; it is not saved to your account. Live location sharing is separate: it is off until you turn it on, it turns off with one tap, and it is never public. You choose whether only you see it or also the people approved for the same activities, and only around the time those activities take place.\n\nWhile live location is on we keep a history of positions for 30 days so you can review and delete it; it is then deleted automatically. You can delete it sooner from your account."),
    ("legal.privacy.providers.title", "Companies that help us"),
    ("legal.privacy.providers.body", "We rely on a small number of service providers who process information only on our instructions: Supabase, for our database, sign-in, and photo storage; Vercel, which hosts the website; Google, only if you choose to sign in with it; and OpenFreeMap, which serves the map tiles your browser loads and therefore receives your IP address and the area of the map you are viewing, without any account information.\n\nWe share information with authorities only when the law requires it, or when we believe in good faith that it is necessary to protect someone's safety."),
    ("legal.privacy.retention.title", "How long we keep it"),
    ("legal.privacy.retention.body", "We keep your account information while your account exists. Live location history is kept for 30 days. Server logs are kept for a short period for security and then deleted. Records of the policies you accepted, your cookie choices, your requests about your information, and moderation decisions are kept as long as the law requires or as needed to defend legal claims, and are then deleted or anonymized."),
    ("legal.privacy.rights.title", "Your choices and rights"),
    ("legal.privacy.rights.body", "From your account settings you can download a copy of your information in a portable format, correct your profile, change who can see you and what notifications you receive, turn location sharing off and delete its history, pause your account, or delete it. You can object to any optional use of your information, and you can change your cookie choices at any time.\n\nWe record each request so we can show it was handled, and we complete it without undue delay. Exercising these rights is free and will never affect how we treat you."),
    ("legal.privacy.deletion.title", "When you delete your account"),
    ("legal.privacy.deletion.body", "Deletion is immediate and cannot be undone. We delete your profile, your photo, your location and its history, your preferences, and your notifications. Upcoming activities you organized are cancelled and their attendees are notified. Past activities remain visible as organized by a deleted member, without your name.\n\nWe keep, separated from your identity, only the records the law requires and those needed to show we honored your consent and requests."),
    ("legal.privacy.security.title", "How we protect it"),
    ("legal.privacy.security.body", "All connections are encrypted. Your session lives in a sealed cookie that no script on the page can read, forms are protected against requests from other sites, and every record in our database is locked so that only you, or the people you allow, can reach it. No system is perfectly secure; if a breach ever affected your information, we would notify you and the authorities as the law requires."),
    ("legal.privacy.minors.title", "Children and teenagers"),
    ("legal.privacy.minors.body", "Boricua Experience is not intended for anyone under 18, and we do not knowingly collect information from minors. Sign-up asks for a date of birth without hinting at the answer; if it shows that a person is under 18, the account is not created, the date is not stored, and that browser cannot try again for a day.\n\nIf we learn that we hold information about a child under 13, we delete it immediately. If we learn that an account belongs to someone under 18, we close the account and delete its information within 30 days, keeping only what the law requires. Parents and guardians can tell us about a minor's account or an activity involving minors by reporting it with the “Involves minors” reason; those reports are reviewed first."),
    ("legal.privacy.transfers.title", "Where it is stored"),
    ("legal.privacy.transfers.body", "Our database and website are hosted in the eastern United States. Puerto Rico is part of the United States, so your information stays under United States law."),
    ("legal.privacy.changes.title", "Changes to this policy"),
    ("legal.privacy.changes.body", "When we change this policy in a way that matters, we will tell you on the platform before the change takes effect and, where the law requires it, ask for your consent again. The version and effective date at the top of this page show which policy applies."),
    ("legal.cookies.title", "Cookie Policy"),
    ("legal.cookies.description", "The cookies and browser storage Boricua Experience uses, what each one does, and how to change your choice."),
    ("legal.cookies.intro", "Cookies are small files your browser keeps so a website can remember something between pages and visits. This page lists each one Boricua Experience uses and why."),
    ("legal.cookies.summary", "We only use cookies the platform needs to work. We use no analytics or advertising cookies today, and if we ever add any, they will stay off until you allow them."),
    ("legal.cookies.what.title", "How we use them"),
    ("legal.cookies.what.body", "All our cookies are first-party, which means they are set by boricuaexperience.com and are only sent back to it. None of them is used to follow you across other websites. Every one of them is marked so that scripts on the page cannot read it, and on the live site they are sent only over encrypted connections."),
    ("legal.cookies.necessary.title", "Cookies the platform needs"),
    ("legal.cookies.necessary.body", "Sign-in session (bx_session) keeps you signed in. It holds your sealed session and lasts up to 30 days, or until you sign out.\n\nSign-in protection (bx_flow) protects a sign-in while it is in progress, for example while you are on Google's page, and expires after 10 minutes.\n\nLanguage preference (bx_lang) remembers the language you chose, for one year.\n\nCookie preference (bx_consent) remembers your cookie choice, for one year, so we do not ask again on every page.\n\nVisitor cookie preference (bx_visitor) is a random identifier, unrelated to your account, that lets us record the cookie choice you made as a visitor. It lasts one year.\n\nConfirmation message (bx_flash) carries a one-time confirmation message, such as “Saved”, to the next page, and disappears within a minute.\n\nBecause the platform cannot work without these, they do not require your consent."),
    ("legal.cookies.storage.title", "Storage in your browser"),
    ("legal.cookies.storage.body", "Live location sharing starts only when you choose it. It stops when you turn it off, hide the page or leave it, and does not resume automatically after a reload. The app caches its public files in your browser so it opens quickly; private account pages are not stored for offline use."),
    ("legal.cookies.optional.title", "Optional cookies"),
    ("legal.cookies.optional.body", "The banner lets you allow analytics cookies, which would help us understand in aggregate how the platform is used, and marketing cookies, which would help us measure campaigns. We use neither today. Your choice is recorded so that, if we ever add them, they only run with your permission."),
    ("legal.cookies.third.title", "Other services"),
    ("legal.cookies.third.body", "The map images are loaded from OpenFreeMap, which does not set cookies. If you choose to sign in with Google, Google may set its own cookies on its own website under its own policies."),
    ("legal.cookies.choices.title", "Changing your choice"),
    ("legal.cookies.choices.body", "You can change your choice at any time with the button below, and we record each change. You can also delete cookies in your browser settings; if you delete bx_session you will be signed out."),
    ("about.title", "About Boricua Experience"),
    ("about.description", "A platform to discover, join, and create activities in Puerto Rico, built on privacy."),
    ("about.intro", "We believe the best of Puerto Rico happens when people get together."),
    ("about.mission.title", "Our mission"),
    ("about.mission.body", "Make finding something to do as easy as searching for it, and hosting something of your own as easy as publishing it: culture, music, sports, workshops, beaches, community, birthdays, and civic causes, in every one of the island's 78 towns."),
    ("about.how.title", "How it works"),
    ("about.how.body", "Search or explore the map. Ask to join, and the organizer decides who goes. Once you are approved you get the exact address and the instructions, and you can see who else is going."),
    ("about.safety.title", "Safety first"),
    ("about.safety.body", "Accounts are for adults 18 and over. Exact addresses stay hidden until the organizer approves you, anyone can report an activity, and reports involving minors are reviewed first."),
    ("about.privacy.title", "Privacy by design"),
    ("about.privacy.body", "Your location is yours: off by default, never public, with a history you can delete. You can download or delete your information at any time.")
  ])
